window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["07"]={"https://theconversation.com/if-australians-dont-trust-the-rba-on-inflation-the-interest-rate-pain-may-have-to-get-worse-296141":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"33da284fd3d6ae19947164270808a616bbe017b997c17d19cd548a95a5e84869","read":"https://theconversation.com/if-australians-dont-trust-the-rba-on-inflation-the-interest-rate-pain-may-have-to-get-worse-296141","bytes":179614,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"If Australians don’t trust the RBA on inflation, the interest rate pain may have to get worse","by":[{"n":"Meg Elkins","r":"Associate Professor in Economics, RMIT University"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T18:23:03Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["As an economist, it’s the question I’m asked wherever I go: “why has the Reserve Bank of Australia lifted interest rates five times this year? Don’t they realise how much pain I am already in?”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Small businesses are also being squeezed as consumers are spending less; borrowing is costing more; and half of small businesses borrowings are ",["linked to their home loans","https://theconversation.com/small-businesses-in-australia-have-a-hard-time-getting-finance-other-countries-offer-a-different-solution-287971"],", which means they are hit twice by the higher rates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public anger has prompted headlines about ",["sacking the RBA","https://x.com/dailytelegraph/status/2117549857632334218"],", while people on social media have been calling the hikes “ ",["a bad joke","https://www.facebook.com/reel/1592657215453973"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["But here’s the risk: the more Australians think we’re losing the fight against inflation, the more the RBA may have to consider another rate hike in the months ahead. Here’s why."]},{"k":"h","s":["The psychology of rising inflation"]},{"k":"p","s":["As my work on ",["inflationary psychology","https://doi.org/10.4337/9781802207736.00081"]," has shown, Australians are currently in a risky situation."]},{"k":"p","s":["We’re experiencing rising prices. Anticipating that price could rise further, we buy more now. That contributes to products or services being scarcer – and leads to further price rises."]},{"k":"p","s":["Higher inflation can become a self-fulfilling prophecy."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research published this month","https://doi.org/10.1257/aer.20250051"]," in the American Economic Review found that consumers in the United States largely ignore inflation below about 4%. This is backed up by previous studies from other regions, including ",["the European Union","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejpoleco.2025.102702"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But once inflation rises above 4%, consumer attention roughly doubles – and inflation expectations start to move with it."]},{"k":"p","s":["With headline inflation (also known as the ",["consumer price index","https://www.rba.gov.au/education/resources/explainers/inflation-and-its-measurement.html"],", or CPI) at 4.3%, Australia has been above that threshold for much of this year."]},{"k":"h","s":["What it means for wages"]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, when the CPI hits 3.5% or higher, as it is now, it ",["can trigger a rule","https://www.hrleader.com.au/learning/26079-public-sector-workers-to-receive-11-4-pay-increase-over-next-3-years"]," in some Australian enterprise bargaining agreements that says workers can try negotiating for a one-off, cost-of-living allowance."]},{"k":"p","s":["So if 3.5%-plus inflation becomes the new normal, many businesses will have to assume they’ll face higher wage demands."]},{"k":"p","s":["If that happens, past experience has shown us that businesses will lift prices to cover those higher wages. Wages and prices can then chase each other in a “ ",["wage-price spiral","https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wage-price-spiral.asp"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, this is less likely to happen than in the past because workers have less bargaining power, with ",["union membership falling","https://theconversation.com/yes-what-you-think-about-inflation-can-influence-what-the-rba-does-next-278549"]," and less frequent wage negotiations."]},{"k":"h","s":["The RBA’s ‘nightmare’ scenario"]},{"k":"p","s":["When people believe the RBA is on target to deliver on keeping inflation under control, businesses aren’t so quick to increase prices."]},{"k":"p","s":["But when businesses and workers stop believing inflation can be reined in, that’s a real problem. The Reserve Bank’s Deputy Governor Andrew Hauser recently warned there are “an increasing share of businesses who are thinking that […] 3%, 3.5% [inflation] is the new normal […] That is the central banker’s nightmare.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The RBA wants to try to keep underlying inflation within its “target band” of 2–3%. But inflation has been above that band for the past five years – and it’s ",["heading up again","https://theconversation.com/inflation-jumps-to-4-3-adding-to-pressure-for-rba-rate-rise-next-week-295162"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why public perceptions matter so much"]},{"k":"p","s":["In another speech this month, Hauser ",["shared the latest data","https://www.rba.gov.au/speeches/2026/sp-dg-2026-11-05.html"]," from four RBA surveys of 12,000 Australians since early 2025. The bank still ranks higher on trust than any level of government."]},{"k":"p","s":["But its surveys show public confidence that it can get inflation back to its 2–3% target has fallen sharply."]},{"k":"p","s":["That fall in confidence came even before the most recent official figures showing ",["higher, persistent inflation","https://theconversation.com/inflation-jumps-to-4-3-adding-to-pressure-for-rba-rate-rise-next-week-295162"],", and November’s interest rate hike."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Melbourne Institute","https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/AMQeq/4/"],"’s latest November survey, released late last week, shows consumer inflation expectations have been rising since July this year. For a second month in a row, Australian householders said they expect to face 5.3% inflation over the coming year – higher than inflation is now."]},{"k":"h","s":["Past evidence on rates and inflation"]},{"k":"p","s":["As the Reserve Bank Governor Michele Bullock has acknowledged, higher rates ",["can’t tame all types of inflation","https://theconversation.com/rba-hikes-interest-rates-to-an-18-year-high-warning-inflation-will-hurt-for-another-year-294682"],", such as global oil prices."]},{"k":"p","s":["The RBA estimates the 2022 rate rises cut household spending between ",["0.4–0.8% a year","https://www.rba.gov.au/speeches/2023/sp-ag-2023-10-11.html"]," and brought business investment down by 4%, both of which helped bring down inflation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unfortunately, there is a time lag. Other ",["RBA research","https://www.rba.gov.au/publications/bulletin/2025/apr/monetary-policy-transmission-through-the-lens-of-the-rbas-models.html"]," shows the effect on inflation peaks one to two years after rates rise."]},{"k":"p","s":["So the one economic “lever” the RBA can control – raising rates to curb inflation – does have an impact. But it’s not perfect, and it does require patience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Yes, what you think about inflation can influence what the RBA does next","https://theconversation.com/yes-what-you-think-about-inflation-can-influence-what-the-rba-does-next-278549"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Potential good news before Christmas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The next RBA announcement on interest rates is on December 8. Financial markets – which largely get it right at predicting the RBA’s moves – are ",["overwhelmingly forecasting","https://www.asx.com.au/markets/trade-our-derivatives-market/futures-market/rba-rate-tracker"]," rates will stay on hold before Christmas. That’s the good news."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Major banks are also forecasting","https://www.news.com.au/finance/economy/interest-rates/mortgage-holders-spared-further-rate-pain-as-housing-downturn-and-spending-slowdown-hit/news-story/fc06f44b76c63f11f78695216d4afd68"]," rates could start to come down again as early as August next year."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, if the RBA gets the sense from future public surveys that Australians think inflation is still out of control, it ",["hasn’t ruled out","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-03/rba-lifts-interest-rates-november-2026-highest-rate-in-18-years/107340050#:%7E:text=In%20her%20post%2Dmeeting%20press%20conference%2C%20RBA%20governor%20Michele%20Bullock%20left%20the%20door%20open%20for%20more%20rate%20increases."]," having to hike rates again."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Inflation is proving more stubborn in Australia than elsewhere, making the RBA’s job harder","https://theconversation.com/inflation-is-proving-more-stubborn-in-australia-than-elsewhere-making-the-rbas-job-harder-295878"]]}],"chars":5066},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/fiji":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"277c5e891cc7e0ec2869c23a3537f24deb691e665214c2157c02152640e843a6","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/fiji","bytes":57957,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Fiji travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-10T14:48:05+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/sri-lanka/british-high-commission-suva"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/fiji/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Fiji’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Fiji set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Fiji High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive in Fiji."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need a visa for visits of up to 4 months. If you plan to stay for longer than 4 months, apply for a visa from the ",["Fiji Immigration Department","https://www.immigration.gov.fj/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Fiji border control, you must also show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["an onward or return ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["a valid visa for the next country you’re travelling to"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting Fiji on business, you must apply for a ",["business visitors permit","https://www.immigration.gov.fj/"],", which is valid for 21 days."]},{"k":"h","s":["Yacht entry"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yachts can only enter Fiji through Suva, Lautoka, Savusavu and Levuka. For other ports, such as Nadi and Denarau, you ",["must have prior agreement from the Fijian authorities","https://www.frcs.org.fj/our-services/customs/yachts-and-vessels/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are entering Fiji on a work or residency permit, and are travelling as a lone parent, you may need to have evidence of your parental responsibility. For further information contact the Fiji High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Fiji, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Fiji guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/79/fiji#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Fiji","https://www.frcs.org.fj/our-services/customs/visiting-fiji/arriving-in-fiji/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fiji customs has strict quarantine regulations and customs officers X-ray all luggage arriving at Nadi airport. They will confiscate most fresh foodstuffs, unless you’re arriving from a country with quarantine agreements with Fiji."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Fiji"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash in any currency worth 10,000 Fijian dollars or more. If you are found with undeclared cash, you could be prosecuted and get a fine or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most tourist hotels and many restaurants accept credit cards. Not all ATMs accept the full range of bank or credit cards. The Australian and New Zealand Bank (ANZ) and Westpac ATMs accept cards with the Visa, Mastercard, Maestro and Cirrus symbols."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Fiji"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Fiji, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests can occur with little warning. Avoid demonstrations, rallies or street gatherings. Avoid any areas of obvious military or police activity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of serious crime is generally low, but there are occasional incidents including sexual assault."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful of your belongings in cities and other popular tourist destinations. To reduce the risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying everything in one bag"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry a copy of the photo page of your passport and leave the original in a secure place"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid leaving your belongings unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["be alert when withdrawing money from cash machines"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep windows and doors locked when driving and belongings out of sight when parked"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take additional care when walking at night in cities, towns and isolated areas, particularly if you are a woman travelling alone. There have been serious sexual assaults against foreign nationals in Fiji, including British women."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to the risk of credit card fraud. This may include credit card skimming devices or other types of data theft. Take care when paying with credit cards or withdrawing money from ATMs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mobile phone coverage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Phone coverage in rural areas and outlying islands can be limited or non-existent. Many UK mobile phones do not work, as your provider may not have an international roaming agreement in Fiji."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can buy a Fiji SIM card at Nadi International Airport and at convenience stores and supermarkets. You must register your SIM card if you buy it locally."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of even small quantities of illegal drugs can lead to imprisonment and a large fine. Possession of any amount of marijuana carries a 3-month prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kava-drinking ceremonies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kava is a traditional drink in Fiji used in kava ceremonies. If you’re invited to take part in a kava-drinking ceremony, be aware of the potential risks of liver toxicity."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Nudity"]},{"k":"p","s":["Topless bathing and nudity in public is illegal. Cover your shoulders and knees in rural villages and during kava ceremonies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Homosexuality was decriminalised in February 2010, but there can be local sensitivities, particularly when visiting rural communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water-based activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are dangerous rip tides along reefs and river estuaries. Unless you have reliable local knowledge, swim from beaches that have lifeguards on duty and follow the flag warning system."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you take part in any water activities, make sure you use a reputable, fully licensed company with up-to-date equipment and necessary safety features."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving schools may have limited resources and do not always observe safety and maintenance standards. Always:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask to see a dive operator’s credentials and use schools with appropriate qualifications and credentials"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the conditions on your insurance policy – some policies require dive instructors to have certain qualifications"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure safety equipment is in good condition"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure oxygen is available on the boat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you know what to do if something goes wrong, including how to call for help while at sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s only one hyperbaric (recompression) chamber in Fiji, at the Colonial War Memorial Hospital in Suva. It is not always working. Check its status before scuba diving and get advice from your dive instructor or dive team. Make sure your insurance covers diving and medical evacuation costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of jellyfish and follow local advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Fiji, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK driving licence to drive in Fiji."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many roads in Fiji are in poor condition and can be dangerous. Roads are particularly hazardous at night due to a lack of street lighting and the chance of pedestrians or stray animals on the road. Avoid road travel outside of urban areas at night. Vehicle safety regulations are rarely enforced and driving standards are poor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Severe weather can lead to roads becoming damaged, blocked or washed away. Seek local advice before you set out."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and minibuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use licensed taxis that have a yellow registration plate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Not all minibuses are licensed. Only use those with yellow number plates. Unlicensed minibuses are frequently not insured."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the boat operator’s credentials and safety equipment before boarding boats or vessels travelling between islands. Avoid any vessels that are overloaded as they are in danger of capsizing or sinking, particularly in poor weather conditions. Check to make sure there is adequate life-saving equipment for everyone on board in case of emergencies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fiji is in an earthquake zone. There can be occasional tremors, which could trigger tsunami alerts. Make sure you understand the local safety procedures for earthquakes and tsunamis."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake or tsunami."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclone season normally runs from November to April, but cyclones occur throughout the year. During the cyclone season there is a greater risk of strong winds and heavy rain. Cyclones can cause flooding and landslides, often damaging or blocking roads and resulting in road closures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow weather updates from Fiji Meteorological Service, local newspapers and Radio Fiji GOLD. The National Disaster Management Office has information on how to prepare."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Fiji","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/79/fiji#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Fiji","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/79/fiji"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"li","s":["HIV/AIDS, and other sexually transmitted infections. For more information, see ",["TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/79/fiji#Outbreaks"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Fiji"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Fiji","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/fiji-doctors-and-medical-facilities/list-of-english-speaking-doctors-and-medical-facilities-in-fiji"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare facilities are limited in range and availability. In serious medical emergencies, people are often evacuated to another country for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no reciprocal healthcare agreement between the UK and Fiji. Hospitals usually ask for immediate cash payment for health services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Fiji"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 910"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Fiji"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Fiji"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Fiji"]," in Fiji"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Fiji","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/fiji-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Fiji","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/fiji-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/fiji/british-high-commission-suva"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/fiji/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":14479,"change":"Removal of information about Tropical Cyclone Vaianu (‘Warnings and Insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/donasi-bencana-karhutla-urunan-warga-bukan-alasan-negara-lepas-tangan-292987":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"7b99540f6608697b471e3c8161fd3203dbe8e2f6fd9cb47c665197995246f5f6","read":"https://theconversation.com/donasi-bencana-karhutla-urunan-warga-bukan-alasan-negara-lepas-tangan-292987","bytes":180011,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Donasi bencana karhutla: Urunan warga bukan alasan negara lepas tangan","by":[{"n":"Arief Rakhman","r":"Pengajar di Jurusan Ilmu Sosial dan Ilmu Politik, Universitas Jambi"}],"pub":"2026-10-09T09:03:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Donasi warga penting, tetapi bukan pengganti kewajiban negara."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Pujian terhadap gotong royong jangan mengaburkan tanggung jawab pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Solidaritas harus berjalan bersama tuntutan akuntabilitas dan pencegahan bencana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Akhir tahun lalu, patungan yang diinisiasi oleh influencer Ferry Irwandi berhasil mengumpulkan ",["Rp10,3 milliar","https://www.tempo.co/politik/ferry-irwandi-kumpulkan-rp-10-miliar-donasi-korban-banjir-sumatera-dalam-waktu-24-jam-2095091"]," hanya dalam 24 jam sejak diumumkan. Aksi serupa juga dilakukan banyak pemuka lain yang peruntukannya adalah untuk membantu korban banjir Sumatra."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada September 2026, gerakan serupa kembali digagas untuk membantu hutan Kalimantan yang terbakar. Donasi terkumpul lebih dari ",["Rp3 miliar","https://megapolitan.kompas.com/read/2026/09/04/19011611/ferry-irwandi-ajak-donasi-hutan-kalimantan-sudah-terkumpul-rp-3-miliar"],", dengan target ",["Rp50 miliar","https://katadata.co.id/ekonomi-hijau/investasi-hijau/6aace1ad033c6/inisiasi-patungan-rp50-miliar-untuk-amankan-hutan-ini-rencana-ferry-irwandi"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Wakil Presiden Gibran Rakabuming Raka","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5295112/gibran-apresiasi-gerakan-ferry-irwandi-sebut-aksi-nyata-gotong-royong"]," bahkan menyebutnya sebagai “aksi nyata dari semangat gotong royong”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kekuatan solidaritas sesama warga ini memang patut diacungi jempol. Namun, kita tetap harus mempertanyakan di mana tanggung jawab kemanusiaan warga berakhir dan tanggung jawab politik negara dimulai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bukan berarti masyarakat tidak boleh berdonasi karena korban bencana membutuhkan pertolongan segera. Mereka tidak bisa menunggu tata ruang diperbaiki, izin dievaluasi, atau penegakan hukum berjalan sebelum mendapat makanan, obat, tempat tinggal, atau bantuan evakuasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalah muncul ketika bantuan warga mulai menggantikan pekerjaan yang seharusnya dilakukan negara. Jangan sampai keberhasilan gerakan sumbangan dari publik dan untuk publik ini justru membuat negara semakin jarang ditagih."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Kenapa donasi banjir Sumatra dari ‘influencer’ cepat meraup dukungan publik?","https://theconversation.com/kenapa-donasi-banjir-sumatra-dari-influencer-cepat-meraup-dukungan-publik-271486"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Menyumbang bukan masalahnya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Riset bencana menunjukkan bahwa jaringan sosial warga penting dalam pemulihan. Ilmuwan politik ",["Daniel Aldrich","https://bibliovault.org/BV.landing.epl?ISBN=9780226012889"],", misalnya, mengungkap hubungan antarwarga merupakan salah satu faktor penting dalam kemampuan masyarakat bangkit setelah bencana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, ",["penelitian","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10911359.2024.2326501"]," tentang gerakan berbagi makanan di Yogyakarta selama pandemi juga menunjukkan bagaimana aksi sukarela warga menopang kelompok rentan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hukum Indonesia pun menempatkan warga dan negara pada posisi yang berbeda. Undang Undang Penanggulangan Bencana ",["memberi warga hak dan kewajiban","https://pasal.id/peraturan/uu/uu-no-24-tahun-2007/pasal-27"]," untuk terlibat, tetapi menetapkan pemerintah dan pemerintah daerah ",["sebagai penanggung jawab utama","https://pasal.id/peraturan/uu/uu-no-24-tahun-2007/pasal-5"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, bantuan warga seharusnya menjadi pelengkap, bukan pengganti."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ferry pun ",["pernah menjelaskan","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F-JJwvzpzB0"]," hal tersebut dengan sederhana–bahwa jika regulator memiliki kewajiban melakukan 100 dan masyarakat membantu dengan 1, kewajiban regulator tetap 100."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalannya justru muncul di ruang publik. Ketika warga membantu menutup kebutuhan yang tidak terpenuhi pemerintah, korban memang tertolong."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, jika respons pemerintah berhenti pada pujian terhadap kedermawanan warga, perhatian publik dapat bergeser: dari menagih mengapa masalah terjadi menjadi merayakan berapa banyak uang yang berhasil dikumpulkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Untuk kebakaran hutan dan lahan, pemerintah memang ",["mengerahkan ribuan personel","https://gakkum.kehutanan.go.id/siaran-pers/detail/kemenhut-kerahkan-12880-personel-gabungan-relawan-dan-masyarakat-untuk-tangani-karhutla-di-kalimantan"]," untuk penanganan karhutla. Namun, selain tanggap penanggulangan, negara tetap harus mencegah kebakaran berulang, mengevaluasi izin, menindak pelanggaran, dan memperbaiki tata kelola lingkungan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Patungan hutan ala Ferry Irwandi: Solusi atau gagal paham akar masalah karhutla?","https://theconversation.com/patungan-hutan-ala-ferry-irwandi-solusi-atau-gagal-paham-akar-masalah-karhutla-277254"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Sembunyi di balik kata ‘gotong royong’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika pejabat menyebut patungan warga sebagai “gotong royong”, terdengarnya positif. Namun, jika tidak disertai penjelasan tentang apa yang sedang dilakukan pemerintah, istilah tersebut berisiko ",["menempatkan negara sebagai penonton","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0263775820976570"]," yang bertepuk tangan atas solidaritas masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Filsuf politik Iris Marion Young","https://academic.oup.com/book/4381?login=false"]," menjelaskan bahwa tanggung jawab atas ketidakadilan struktural memang dapat dipikul bersama, tetapi tidak berarti semua pihak memiliki tanggung jawab yang sama besar. Mereka yang memiliki lebih banyak kekuasaan dan sumber daya memikul tanggung jawab lebih besar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam konteks bencana, warga dapat menyumbang Rp10 ribu atau Rp10 juta, tetapi mereka tidak memiliki kewenangan mencabut izin konsesi, menegakkan hukum, mengatur tata ruang, atau menentukan anggaran negara. Kewenangan itu ada pada ",["pemerintah","https://www.refworld.org/legal/resolution/unga/1992/20488"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, gotong royong tidak boleh menjadi bahasa yang membuat kewajiban negara terdengar seperti pekerjaan sukarela."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Aksi kritis di media sosial kian masif, tapi kurang memberikan perubahan nyata","https://theconversation.com/aksi-kritis-di-media-sosial-kian-masif-tapi-kurang-memberikan-perubahan-nyata-282058"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Tiga pertanyaan untuk menandai batas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ada setidaknya tiga pertanyaan yang dapat diajukan setiap kali kampanye donasi bencana menjadi viral."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertama, apakah donasi ini menjawab kebutuhan darurat atau menggantikan fungsi dasar negara?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Makanan, obat, evakuasi, dan tempat tinggal sementara jelas membutuhkan solidaritas segera. Namun, jika masyarakat harus patungan untuk membangun kembali fasilitas publik atau memulihkan hutan yang rusak, publik perlu bertanya mengapa fungsi tersebut tidak sepenuhnya dijalankan melalui kebijakan dan anggaran negara."]},{"k":"p","s":["UU Penanggulangan Bencana pun menempatkan ",["pemulihan pascabencana","https://pasal.id/peraturan/uu/uu-no-24-tahun-2007/pasal-26"]," sebagai tanggung jawab pemerintah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua, apakah pejabat berbicara sebagai pihak yang ditagih atau sebagai penonton?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Warga memiliki hak untuk memperoleh informasi dan mengawasi pelaksanaan penanggulangan bencana. Karena itu, ketika miliaran rupiah terkumpul dari masyarakat, respons pemerintah seharusnya bukan hanya “terima kasih” atau pujian atas gotong royong."]},{"k":"p","s":["Publik juga berhak mendapat jawaban: bagaimana pemerintah mencegah bencana serupa, mengevaluasi izin, menindak pelanggaran, dan menggunakan anggaran pencegahan?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketiga, apakah percakapan berhenti pada angka donasi atau berlanjut ke penyebab bencana?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sepanjang Januari hingga Juli 2026, Walhi mencatat ",["74% titik panas","https://www.betahita.id/berita/12223/25-524-titik-panas-di-kalimantan-berada-di-konsesi-perusahaan"]," di Kalimantan berada di wilayah konsesi perusahaan. Bencana bukan sekadar peristiwa alam, melainkan mencerminkan ",["kegagalan pembangunan dan tata kelola","https://www.preventionweb.net/publication/risk-natural-hazards-peoples-vulnerability-and-disasters"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, donasi seharusnya memiliki dua arah: satu tangan membantu korban, tangan lainnya menunjuk pihak yang memiliki kewenangan untuk mencegah bencana berikutnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kemarau akan kembali. Musim hujan akan kembali. Banjir, kebakaran, dan bencana lain juga akan kembali menguji solidaritas warga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Warga hampir pasti akan kembali bergotong royong–dan itu baik. Yang tidak boleh ikut berulang adalah pola ketika negara menerima pujian atas gotong royong masyarakat, sementara kewajibannya sendiri tidak ikut dibicarakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ferry sudah memberi hitungannya: kewajiban negara tetap 100, berapa pun yang disumbangkan warga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jadi, di mana tanggung jawab kemanusiaan warga berakhir dan tanggung jawab politik negara dimulai? Mungkin tepat setelah ucapan terima kasih."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ketika negara gagal menjamin rasa aman, warga bisa melihat pemerintah sebagai ancaman","https://theconversation.com/ketika-negara-gagal-menjamin-rasa-aman-warga-bisa-melihat-pemerintah-sebagai-ancaman-290937"]]}],"chars":6511},"https://theconversation.com/lebanons-power-sharing-formula-was-once-a-model-for-conflict-resolution-now-it-is-creaking-293991":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"a49fc4976e641a5da120cadbe879da78eb88455b60dda2ad6ae308aa22e400ba","read":"https://theconversation.com/lebanons-power-sharing-formula-was-once-a-model-for-conflict-resolution-now-it-is-creaking-293991","bytes":191268,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Lebanon’s power‑sharing formula was once a model for conflict resolution – now it is creaking","by":[{"n":"Tamirace Fakhoury","r":"Associate Professor of International Politics and Conflict, Tufts University"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T13:37:06Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["“ ",["No one speaks on behalf of Lebanon","https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/09/1168444"],",” declared the nation’s prime minister, Nawaf Salam, at the United Nations General Assembly in September 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Decisions of war and peace, he continued, belong solely to the Lebanese state. Salam went on to call for a consolidated ceasefire between Israel and Hezbollah, the Shiite political party with a military arsenal, along with the withdrawal of Israeli troops and the implementation of ",["U.N. Resolution 1701","https://unsco.unmissions.org/sites/default/files/s_res_17012006.pdf"],", which seeks to establish a weapons-free zone in Lebanon’s south."]},{"k":"p","s":["The speech was meant to signal to the international community that the government is working to reassert state authority. But back home, many Lebanese saw a large gap between the lofty rhetoric of state authority and ",["the realities","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/25/israeli-shelling-continues-as-lebanons-pm-demands-withdrawal-in-un-speech"]," on the ground."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the past two years, ",["violence has radically transformed","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/6/nearly-9000-killed-in-israeli-attacks-on-lebanon-since-2023"]," the villages and landscapes of Lebanon’s south. Even before then, many Lebanese felt a chasm between the people and the country’s leadership: a perceived failure of the state to act on various issues, from the ",["2020 Beirut port explosion","https://www.hrw.org/news/2023/08/03/lebanon-3-years-no-justice-beirut-blast"]," to ",["the collapse of the country’s currency and financial sector","https://www.reuters.com/markets/rates-bonds/lebanons-financial-crisis-how-it-happened-2022-01-23/"]," and ",["the fragile security situation","https://theconversation.com/israel-and-lebanon-have-a-long-history-of-failed-ceasefires-will-this-time-be-any-different-286515"],". Now, to many in the country, Lebanon has been dragged into ",["unbalanced negotiations","https://religionandsecurity.org/2026/04/24/lebanons-weaker-negotiating-position/"]," with Israel from a position of ",["weakness","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/23/mixed-views-in-lebanon-ahead-of-controversial-talks-with-israel"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a ",["scholar who focuses on the dynamics of Lebanon’s politics","https://fletcher.tufts.edu/academics/faculty/tamirace-fakhoury"],", I fear that the crises that have befallen Lebanon have placed greater strain on Lebanon’s already fragile ",["power-sharing system","https://www.france24.com/en/20200901-cause-of-all-ills-lebanon-s-complex-power-sharing-system"],", which depends on coexistence among 18 officially recognized sectarian communities. Now more than 80 years old, the arrangement was once held up as a model for countries around the world that are split along ethnoreligious lines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Lebanon’s power-sharing formula"]},{"k":"p","s":["At its core, Lebanon’s political system ",["rests on a formula","https://www.britannica.com/event/Lebanese-National-Pact-1943"]," in which communities divide political authority among themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":["Its roots reach back to Ottoman rule, but Lebanese elites reaffirmed it in its modern form twice: in 1943, as the country emerged from ",["the French mandate","https://www.britannica.com/place/Lebanon/French-mandate"],", and in 1989, with the ",["Taif Agreement","https://www.un.int/lebanon/sites/www.un.int/files/Lebanon/the_taif_agreement_english_version_.pdf"]," that ended the Lebanese civil war."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under its provisions, the agreement allows for the three main political executive positions to be shared among the three largest groups, with a Maronite Christian president, a Shiite speaker of parliament and a Sunni prime minister. In the parliament, seats are divided equally among Lebanon’s diverse Muslim and Christian denominations; civil service appointments are also structured around sectarian quotas."]},{"k":"p","s":["For analysts of conflict resolution in deeply divided societies, Lebanon is one of the key cases that inspired the theory of power-sharing developed in the 1960s by political scientists such as the Dutch American ",["Arend Lijphart","https://polisci.ucsd.edu/people/faculty/faculty-directory/emeriti-faculty/lijphart-profile.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The theory has since become ",["a major framework","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/government-and-opposition/article/what-do-we-know-about-power-sharing-after-50-years/7D60EFF22ADEB3AD3BFAC89E8BB6D519"]," for understanding conflict resolution in societies divided along ethnonational and sectarian lines. It has been applied in ",["Northern Ireland","https://www.taylorfrancis.com/books/edit/10.4324/9781003530978/consociational-power-sharing-northern-ireland-timofey-agarin-rupert-taylor"],", Italian autonomous province ",["South Tyrol","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13537113.2018.1489486"],", ",["Bosnia-Herzegovina","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13537113.2026.2622180"],", ",["Iraq","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13537113.2025.2558053"]," and ",["Burundi","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/000203970904400304"],". It has also been proposed for the post-civil war transition in ",["Syria","https://www.giga-hamburg.de/en/publications/giga-focus/syria-power-sharing-as-an-alternative-to-regional-conflagration"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At its core, the model rests on what I call “dual avoidance.” This lets warring parties avoid partitioning the country while allowing communities to avoid forced assimilation. They can, for instance, retain control over their own languages, traditions and educational and religious institutions. One scholar ",["equates it to","https://doi.org/10.1080/17449050701345041"]," “living apart in the same room.”"]},{"k":"h","s":["Power-sharing risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Lebanon, this arrangement has enabled a fragile coexistence that has been tested many times, with the ",["Israel-Hezbollah war","https://apnews.com/article/israel-hezbollah-conflict-timeline-a2f7978dee7f29af1d50f690d032e4d3"]," that began Oct. 8, 2023, representing the latest."]},{"k":"p","s":["That war, now intertwined with the broader regional confrontation involving ",["Iran and the United States","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/confrontation-between-united-states-and-iran"],", has taken a heavy toll on the authority of the Lebanese government. It has exposed the state’s structural vulnerabilities, while reopening ",["debates","https://worldpeacefoundation.org/blog/lebanon-where-is-the-state/"]," about the performance of Lebanon’s sectarian political system in managing domestic and external challenges."]},{"k":"p","s":["Three major risks in particular look set to shape the future of power-sharing in the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["1. The risk of disarmament"]},{"k":"p","s":["The question of Hezbollah’s military arsenal has been a perennial challenge for Lebanese state formation."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2004, U.N. ",["Security Resolution 1559","https://docs.un.org/en/S/RES/1559(2004)"]," called for the disarmament of all nonstate groups in the country, yet Hezbollah has consistently refused to give up its arms, ",["citing various reasons","https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1470010/hezbollah-will-not-give-up-its-strength-remains-ready-to-confront-israel-qassem.html"]," including what it views as ongoing Israeli threats. Yet that disarmament was a stipulation of the June 2026 ",["trilateral framework","https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2026/06/trilateral-framework-between-the-united-states-of-america-the-state-of-israel-and-the-republic-of-lebanon/"]," between Lebanon and Israel that was meant to pave the way for future bilateral relations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The attempted disarmament has sparked a vociferous debate, not only about Hezbollah’s arsenal but about ",["the terms","https://www.nouvelobs.com/opinions/20260424.OBS114440/guerre-et-paix-au-liban-face-au-desastre-humanitaire-negociations-divisions-contradictions.html."]," on which Lebanon is negotiating disarmament with Israel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many ",["fear","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/6/28/in-lebanon-framework-agreement-signed-with-israel-spurs-protest-criticism"]," that Lebanon is bargaining from a position of extreme weakness and that such imbalance will yield only a weaker state, stripped of sovereign decision-making. Here, conflict research offers a cautious reminder: ",["Negotiations","https://academic.oup.com/edited-volume/34361/chapter-abstract/291480170?redirectedFrom=fulltext"]," conducted under asymmetry tend not to address root causes. Instead, they may breed frustration that lays the groundwork for renewed conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["The negotiations between Lebanon and Israel are ",["deadlocked","https://www.arabnews.com/middle-east/lebanon-awaits-impact-of-us-israeli-elections-on-stalled-talks-3010715"],". Hezbollah insists on a full Israeli withdrawal, while Israel conditions its withdrawal on Hezbollah’s disarmament and other security guarantees."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time, many experts question whether the ",["Lebanese army","https://www.globalfirepower.com/"]," ",["would be able to","https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/lebanons-military-can-barely-fighteven-after-3-billion-from-the-u-s-a1d24969"]," redeploy effectively to southern Lebanon and consolidate security in such a deeply polarized environment. These concerns come at a time when the U.N. peacekeeping mission in the country, UNIFIL, is ",["drawing down","https://x.com/UNIFIL_/status/2118347231799460055"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["While some ",["view","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cp8ddydl18vo"]," the current moment as an opportunity to reduce Hezbollah’s influence over Lebanese politics, there are also broad concerns that efforts to disarm Hezbollah under pressure could revive ",["long-standing","https://d1wqtxts1xzle7.cloudfront.net/59106196/Winter_Shiites_of_Lebanon-pages-1-19-libre.pdf"]," perceptions of marginalization within the Shiite community and unsettle the state’s already ",["fragile","https://mecouncil.org/blog_posts/can-lebanon-negotiate-an-end-to-war-without-a-national-consensus/"]," political equilibrium."]},{"k":"h","s":["2. The risk of transactional politics"]},{"k":"p","s":["The strength of the Lebanese state is also undermined by the increasing prominence of a transactional vision of Lebanon’s political future ",["by political elites and international mediators","https://nowlebanon.com/the-experienced-men-who-negotiated-lebanons-decline/"],", privileging quick fixes over substantive reforms."]},{"k":"p","s":["One example is the potential bargaining over the sectarian quota system. An idea being floated as a concession to Hezbollah’s disarming ",["is increasing the decision-making role","https://themedialine.org/mideast-mindset/what-guarantees-does-hezbollah-want-in-exchange-for-its-weapons/"]," that the Shiite community would play in Lebanon’s power-sharing system. Others have suggested that securing the buy-in of the Shiite community would require a ",["sticks-and-carrots","https://today.lorientlejour.com/article/1467804/barrack-says-if-shiites-get-something-from-hezbollahs-disarmament-they-will-cooperate.html"]," approach, including financial packages to reconstruct southern Lebanon."]},{"k":"p","s":["These ideas conflate historical ",["security dilemmas","https://www.jstor.org/stable/2539070"]," posed by Israeli occupation and Hezbollah armament and the ",["intractable","https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/intractable-conflicts/2A451C32084DD869D4AD67BE74526F52"]," Israeli-Palestinian conflict, which has had various spillovers in Lebanon, with adjustments to political formulas or the reconstruction of aid packages."]},{"k":"p","s":["They also risk reducing disarmament to a matter of bargaining over shares of political power. But they do little to address the underlying drivers of mistrust and the legacies of inequalities in Lebanon."]},{"k":"h","s":["3. The risk of social breakdown"]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, Lebanon’s power-sharing system is increasingly buffeted by the breakdown of social cohesion. Massive ",["internal displacement","https://news.un.org/en/story/2026/07/1168003"]," as families have fled areas under Israeli attack have tested the limits of intercommunal coexistence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lebanon, which spent years scrambling to ",["formulate policies","https://www.socialsciences-centre.org/english/research/articles/list/paper/official-response-syrian-refugee-crisis-lebanon-disastrous-policy-no-policy"]," for refugees displaced by the Syrian civil war that started in 2011, now finds itself contending with a situation that since 2023 has seen more than ",["a million people","https://www.refugeesinternational.org/events-and-testimony/lebanon-at-a-breaking-point-conflict-displacement-and-the-regional-protection-crisis/"]," displaced, mainly from the Shiite-dominated south."]},{"k":"p","s":["This internal displacement raises profound questions about people’s readiness to share ",["divided spaces","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/mass-displacement-lebanon-war-revives-spectre-sectarian-strife-2024-10-15"]," in times of crisis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many households took displaced families into their homes, and communities set up spontaneous reception centers. Yet, in some areas, displaced people from the south came to be seen as a liability, and neighborhoods came up with their own informal security arrangements to monitor the “ ",["coming and going","https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2024/11/12/bayssour-the-druze-village-in-solidarity-with-displaced-shiites-in-southern-lebanon_6732502_4.html"],"” of so-called “outsiders.”"]},{"k":"h","s":["Looking ahead"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taif Agreement turned 37 on Nov. 4, 2026. But can the power-sharing model withstand the strain now bearing down on it, or is Lebanon approaching a reckoning with a formula that can be traced back more than 80 years?"]},{"k":"p","s":["From my perspective, the challenges facing the Lebanese state are immense. They span security, the rebuilding of sovereign decision-making and the restoration of state institutions and infrastructure. They also require navigating a ruthless regional environment amid external pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet I believe these challenges are not insurmountable. They can be addressed if the state does not lose sight of the original impetus that brought Lebanon’s communities together: the desire to craft politics through coexistence."]}],"chars":8874},"https://theconversation.com/yemens-houthis-are-bringing-their-war-to-saudi-arabia-and-reframing-the-narrative-of-being-an-iranian-proxy-294208":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"724eed1fa2978f052178a1fd2e8993d15d54cc489e0c3b70e7abcc453cdd6670","read":"https://theconversation.com/yemens-houthis-are-bringing-their-war-to-saudi-arabia-and-reframing-the-narrative-of-being-an-iranian-proxy-294208","bytes":193669,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Yemen’s Houthis are bringing their war to Saudi Arabia – and reframing the narrative of being an Iranian proxy","by":[{"n":"Laurent Bonnefoy","r":"CNRS research fellow, Center for International Studies, Sciences Po"}],"pub":"2026-10-14T17:57:45Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A ",["deadly Houthi attack","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/10/world/middleeast/riyadh-airport-attack-energy-congress.html"]," on Riyadh’s international airport has highlighted how the Yemeni group is reframing its perceived “Iran proxy” role and shifting its regional focus to its ongoing battle against Saudi Arabia. The Oct. 10 strike, in which 13 people were killed and hundreds injured, was the most violent episode on Saudi Arabian soil since the beginning of the war in Iran in February."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was followed by ",["further – albeit","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-13/saudi-arabia-intercepts-new-houthi-attacks-as-conflict-drags-on?cmpid=101326_morningamer&utm_campaign=morningamer&utm_medium=email&utm_source=newsletter&utm_term=261013&utm_content=10016"]," ",["less deadly","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/yemens-houthis-renew-warning-over-saudi-airports-after-deadly-riyadh-attack-2026-10-11/"]," – ",["missile barrages","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/13/world/middleeast/saudi-arabia-yemen-houthis-aramco-threat.html"]," in the days since. The violence, moreover, comes just as the ",["kingdom is hosting a major conference","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/13/business/saudi-arabia-houthi-oil.html"]," for oil producers."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a longtime ",["analyst of Yemeni politics","https://www.sciencespo.fr/ceri/en/directory/bonnefoy-laurent/"],", I see the latest attacks as another illustration of both the expanding regional stalemate across the Middle East and the need to understand how Yemen’s decade-long war is having effects far beyond its territory."]},{"k":"h","s":["Houthi narratives"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Houthi movement","https://theconversation.com/who-are-yemens-houthis-106423"]," first emerged as a militarized political actor in Yemen in 2004 and has been locked in a multiyear civil war against the internationally recognized, Saudi-backed central government. Currently, the Houthis control about a third of the territory and two-thirds of the population. They are undoubtedly Yemen’s most powerful armed force, despite lacking access to warplanes, and have developed an arsenal of long-range missiles and drones."]},{"k":"p","s":["All along, the Houthis have ",["frequently been portrayed","https://www.bloomsbury.com/uk/sectarianism-desectarianization-and-regional-politics-in-the-middle-east-9780755639212/"]," by their adversaries and many external observers as a proxy for Iran, the chief regional rival to Saudi Arabia."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s true that the movement has ",["long been broadly aligned with Tehran","https://academic.oup.com/ia/article-abstract/92/3/647/2326947"]," and frequently shared regional objections, ",["even if the relationship is complex and varied","https://sanaacenter.org/the-yemen-review/april-june-2026/28082"],". At the same time, the evolution of the Houthi movement remains intimately connected to Yemen’s ",["domestic political context","https://hurstpublishers.com/book/tribes-and-politics-in-yemen/"]," and to a historical feud specific to the country – ",["something I and many other scholars","https://hurstpublishers.com/book/yemen-and-the-world/"]," have researched."]},{"k":"p","s":["What is particularly significant in the current context of an escalating fight with Saudi Arabia, however, is the way in which the Houthi leadership has sought to reframe its military engagement over the course of 2026 so that it does not appear to be directed by Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["This shift is analytically important because it reveals how Houthi leaders ",["understand the political effectiveness","https://www.bloomsbury.com/uk/huthi-movement-in-yemen-9780755644285/"]," of particular narratives and how they seek to legitimize their actions."]},{"k":"h","s":["A belated return to war"]},{"k":"p","s":["When the United States and Israel launched their attack on Iran on Feb. 28, many observers expected the Houthis to enter the conflict swiftly. Their previous ",["intervention in the Red Sea","https://orientxxi.info/the-houthis-in-yemen-gain-the-world-s-attention,6988"]," – between November 2023 and May 2025 – in support of Palestinians after Israel’s war in Gaza had, to some extent, provided a blueprint for ",["disrupting maritime traffic","https://atlasinstitute.org/the-red-sea-shipping-crisis-2024-2025-houthi-attacks-and-global-trade-disruption/"]," through the Strait of Hormuz."]},{"k":"p","s":["The symbolic returns of their earlier campaign had been considerable. On the one hand, it demonstrated the Houthis’ willingness to act in support of Gaza at a time when many Arab governments were ",["widely perceived as turning their backs","https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2026/6/29/why-the-arab-league-could-not-stop-israels-genocide"]," on the plight of Palestinians. It also revealed the movement’s capacity to disrupt global supply chains and affect international trade far beyond Yemen."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the Houthis remained on the sidelines for several months after the initial U.S.-Israeli strikes on Iran. Their leaders appeared to disregard reports that Iranian decision-makers ",["had called on them","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/iran-tells-houthis-close-red-sea-gateway-if-us-hits-power-network-sources-say-2026-07-16/"],", in July 2026, to close the Strait of Bab el-Mandeb to maritime traffic."]},{"k":"p","s":["Assuming that the Houthis would automatically act at Tehran’s command reflected a misreading of Yemeni history and of the identity markers that shape the movement’s political legitimacy. Acting in support of Palestinians could be framed for a domestic and regional audience as an expression of Arab solidarity. But acting on behalf of Iran, a non-Arab Persian country composed almost entirely of ",["Twelver Shia Muslims","https://theconversation.com/twelver-shiism-a-branch-of-islam-that-serves-both-as-a-spiritual-and-political-force-in-iran-and-beyond-259853"],", was considerably more difficult to rationalize in Arab Yemen where Twelver Shia Muslims are absent and Sunnis are the majority."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Houthis’ reentry into the regional conflict in August took place alongside a shift in their political narrative, which increasingly centered on their long-standing adversary, Saudi Arabia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although the strategic consequences of their actions may ultimately benefit Iran in its own regional and international conflicts, the Houthis see their military campaign against Saudi Arabia chiefly as an act of national defense."]},{"k":"h","s":["An earlier airport bombing"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the summer of 2026, an important episode went largely unnoticed in the Western media: the Houthis’ attempt to ",["establish the reopening","https://sanaacenter.org/publications/perspectives-and-analyses/27981"]," of Sanaa International Airport through the surprise departure of a Tehran-bound flight and its subsequent return."]},{"k":"p","s":["The airport, located in the Houthi-controlled capital, had been closed since late 2024 following ",["Israeli strikes","https://www.newarab.com/news/israeli-strikes-shut-down-sanaa-airport-cause-500m-damages"],". Its continued closure meant that access to and exit from Houthi-controlled territory remained subject to restrictions imposed by the movement’s adversaries. These included the authorities controlling Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognized government."]},{"k":"p","s":["From the Houthis’ perspective, their sovereignty consequently remained incomplete. The airport’s closure not only restricted civilian movement but also limited their ability to send supporters abroad for training and potentially to receive military equipment. On July 13, the Saudi military’s ",["subsequent bombing","https://www.reutersconnect.com/item/moment-iranian-plane-lands-in-yemens-hudaydah-after-strike-on-sanaa-airport-2/dGFnOnJldXRlcnMuY29tLDIwMjY6bmV3c21sX09XQU5BQ0FBVklERU8yMDI2MDcxMzQxOTY1NDY4"]," of the Sanaa runway, as the incoming aircraft from Tehran approached, provided the movement an opportunity to reignite its confrontation with Riyadh."]},{"k":"p","s":["After more than three years of a de facto ceasefire and difficult negotiations, Riyadh appeared, as in its dealings with Iran, ",["increasingly eager to extricate itself","https://www.crisisgroup.org/cmt/middle-east-north-africa/yemen-saudi-arabia/yemens-war-returning"]," from the region’s protracted conflicts. Sensing an opening, the Houthi leadership responded by invoking a logic of tit-for-tat retaliation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Houthis’ tactics today are a kind of mirror to the ",["2015 launch of a Saudi-led bombing campaign","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-29319423"]," and blockade of the Houthi-controlled parts of Yemen that has led to years of protracted civil war. The Houthis now claim the right to impose reciprocal restrictions on Saudi Arabia, particularly by targeting its ports and oil-exporting infrastructure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Saudi’s Houthi blowback"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Houthis’ new tactic serves two purposes. First, it allows the Houthis to ",["redirect responsibility","https://sanaacenter.org/publications/perspectives-and-analyses/28309"]," for the economic and humanitarian crisis in and around Sanaa toward the Saudi-enforced blockade rather than their own governance failures, mismanagement and corruption. Second, it provides a rationale for escalating the conflict across the region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Previously, the Houthi military leadership had ",["halted attacks","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/11/11/yemens-houthis-appear-to-pull-back-from-red-sea-shipping-attacks"]," on Israeli-linked shipping in the Red Sea following the formal Gaza ceasefire of October 2025, despite having repeatedly come under bombardment. It had likewise suspended attacks on American vessels following an ",["agreement with the Trump administration","https://www.reuters.com/world/trump-says-us-will-stop-bombing-houthis-after-agreement-struck-2025-05-06/"]," in May 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["These decisions demonstrated a ",["degree of pragmatism","https://theconversation.com/america-is-the-mother-of-terrorism-why-the-houthis-new-slogan-is-important-for-understanding-the-middle-east-222865"]," beneath the movement’s inflammatory rhetoric. That pragmatism appeared to persist even as the Houthis resumed their regional military engagement, with American diplomats reportedly ",["meeting Houthi representatives in Oman","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-officials-met-iran-backed-houthis-oman-over-weekend-sources-say-2026-09-16/"]," in September 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["With Saudi Arabia, however, the Houthis felt less compunction. Riyadh was already facing repeated barrages of Iran missiles as a consequences of its alliance with the U.S. and facing an energy export squeeze. So with the Saudi airport incident, the Houthi leadership feels it ",["has trapped Saudi Arabia","https://theconversation.com/rapid-houthi-advances-in-yemen-pose-massive-strategic-risks-for-saudi-arabia-in-the-gulf-292070"],", with consequences extending to the global economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["This retaliatory strategy was bolstered by ",["successful Houthi moves","https://sanaacenter.org/publications/perspectives-and-analyses/28317"]," in early September to establish a degree of control over the Strait of Bab el-Mandeb, one of the world’s most important maritime choke points. That gave the Houthis leverage over shipping crucial for Saudi Arabia in the Red Sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drones and ballistic missiles, as the attacks on the Riyadh airport illustrate, also give the movement the ",["capacity to strike targets","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/11/why-are-houthi-missiles-breaking-through-saudi-arabias-air-defences"]," across much of Saudi Arabia."]},{"k":"p","s":["The targeting of civilian infrastructure in Saudi Arabia, particularly airports, illustrates the retaliatory logic the Houthis have invoked to justify their actions."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s far from clear what the consequences of this increasingly aggressive Houthi campaign will be. The region seems poised for ongoing strife, and it’s an open question whether it will draw back in the likes of the U.S., which has been reluctant to return to full-scale regional conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet none of that should obscure the plight of civilians in Yemen. Rather, it should serve as a reminder of the suffering of a population exhausted by a war that has lasted for more than a decade and has devastated the already meager infrastructure of ",["what was the poorest country","https://saqibooks.com/books/saqi/yemen-in-crisis/"]," in the Middle East even before the conflict started."]}],"chars":8699},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"844bbc22be96af5aa6c397395321ce148b1f3bcd8db346bb8467f6a82397a436","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar","bytes":67933,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Madagascar travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-16T10:56:40+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Madagascar’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Madagascar set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Embassy of Madagascar in London","https://www.mdg-london.org/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Madagascar, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive. It must also have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Madagascar for up to 15 days without a visa. You must pay a 10-euro administration fee on arrival and be ready to show your onward or return tickets."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to stay longer than 15 days, you can buy a 30- or 60-day single-entry tourist visa on arrival at the airport with US dollars, euros or Malagasy ariary."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also apply in advance to the ",["Embassy of Madagascar in London","https://www.mdg-london.org/"]," for a tourist or immigrant visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can extend either of these visas to a maximum total stay of 90 days while you are in Madagascar. If you overstay, you may be detained or deported."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["A child aged 17 or under, travelling without one or either parent must carry written authorisation from the absent parent or parents when leaving Madagascar."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Madagascar, you must have a certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine in some circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Madagascar guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/134/madagascar#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health screening"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cholera"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are entering Madagascar from a ",["Cholera-affected country","https://www.afro.who.int/health-topics/cholera"],", you may be asked by airport authorities to take an anti-cholera drug (Doxcyline). Anyone who is unable to take Doxcyline should be offered an alternative medication by the health authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternative medication will be provided to those that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["are pregnant"]},{"k":"li","s":["are under 8 years old"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a pre existing medical condition"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are likely to be asked to leave contact details with the health authorities and they may follow up with you after 3-5 days."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Madagascar has introduced additional health measures in response to the Ebola outbreak."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have been in or transited through Kenya or Nigeria in the last 21 days, you must complete and sign a health undertaking and will be subject to regular telephone health monitoring after arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have been in or transited through the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the last 21 days, you may not be allowed to enter Madagascar. You must declare your recent travel history and may be subject to health screening on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can enter Madagascar after travelling from or transiting through the Democratic Republic of Congo if you are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a Malagasy national"]},{"k":"li","s":["a foreign resident"]},{"k":"li","s":["a holder of a valid work or student visa"]},{"k":"li","s":["a diplomat"]},{"k":"li","s":["a member of staff of an international organisation or non-governmental organisation"]},{"k":"p","s":["If this applies to you, you must complete 21 days of quarantine and health monitoring at an approved location. You must pay for your accommodation, food and transport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Madagascar. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into and out of Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take in any food, including fruit, as this is illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["When leaving Madagascar you may, after declaring and showing receipts, take out:"]},{"k":"li","s":["up to 2kg of vanilla"]},{"k":"li","s":["up to 1kg of pepper or cloves"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may only export other plant and animal products if you get permission."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take up to 400,000 Malagasy ariary into Madagascar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare foreign cash or travellers cheques if the value is 7,500 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Madagascar","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Madagascar, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["In late September and early October 2025, significant protests took place in Antananarivo and other parts of Madagascar, which included incidences of violence and looting. A new transitional government was formally established on 17 October. Politically linked rallies are possible and occur in any parts of the country. Avoid large gatherings and political demonstrations as protests can sometimes turn violent. Roads may be closed in response to demonstrations as clashes have been known to occur between security forces and the community."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Africa Corps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia’s ‘Africa Corps’, a paramilitary group directed by the Russian state, is present in Madagascar and its armed forces may be visible in Antananarivo and other parts of the country. ‘Africa Corps’ operates in several African countries, exploiting instability through malign and violent activity to expand Russian influence and advance its interests."]},{"k":"p","s":["On occasion, ‘Africa Corps’ may carry out security functions normally undertaken by the local authorities, in breach of norms of international sovereignty. Take care if approached or stopped by ‘Africa Corps’ personnel and remain non-confrontational."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Robberies and thefts are commonplace throughout Madagascar. Foreigners are targets for pickpockets and muggers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches and islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been violent robberies and assaults even in the daytime, be aware of this risk if you visit isolated and remote beaches, especially alone. Get local advice or use an experienced travel operator when visiting any beach. This could happen in many popular coastal locations including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nosy Be island"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ankify Port"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ambanja"]},{"k":"li","s":["beaches to the south and north of Toliara (Tuléar)"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce the risk of street crime:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not walk alone in city centres or poorly lit urban areas after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["use pre-booked taxis or hotel transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["be alert even in nature reserves, national parks and beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of people approaching you in an over-friendly manner"]},{"k":"li","s":["be on the alert for criminals acting in pairs"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not use your mobile or show cash while on the street"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent armed robberies on main roads, particularly at night and outside major towns. Where possible, drive in a convoy . Either use a recognised tour operator or ask your hotel to arrange transport. Always keep car doors locked and windows closed, particularly in Antananarivo."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar/regional-risks"]," to find out which roads are particularly dangerous."]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of robbery, avoid using multi-passenger taxi vans (‘taxi-brousses’ or ‘bush taxis’). If you’re attacked in any vehicle, do not resist or argue as the criminal could be armed. Stay calm and agree to their demands."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are stopped by security personnel or police, ask for ID as there have been reports of criminals falsely claiming to be police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Report any incident to the police if possible. Take a copy of the police report if you need it for an insurance claim."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnaps"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been occasional instances of criminal kidnapping for ransom in Madagascar, targeting individuals (normally Malagasy nationals) perceived to be wealthy."]},{"k":"p","s":["When arranging business meetings use a secure location. Be aware of your surroundings and always let someone you trust know your whereabouts, especially after dark. If you are a victim of kidnapping, follow the kidnapper’s instructions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Local taboos (‘fady’)"]},{"k":"p","s":["In many parts of Madagascar, aspects of daily life are regulated by taboos, known as ‘fady’. These vary from one region to another. Fady can range from forbidden foods to restrictions on clothing."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to visit remote rural areas, get advice from your tour operator or a local guide. They can advise you about how to behave in certain locations."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan a longer stay in a village, first check if you should inform the head of the local authority (‘Fokontany’) and the village head or wise man (‘Ray aman-dreny’)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport with you, as police randomly make ID checks and do not always accept copies. Keep a copy of your passport’s photo page, visa and insurance details somewhere safe, and leave further copies with family or friends in the UK."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Paying for sex is illegal. The penalty is a fine of 1,500 to 7,000 euros and possibly a prison sentence of up to 10 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["The law against sexual abuse of underage children (aged 17 and under) is strictly enforced, especially for incidents that involve foreign tourists. Underage sex workers may carry fake identity cards. In this situation, you could be prosecuted, or an attempt could be made to extort a bribe from you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug smuggling is a serious offence. Punishments can be severe and prison conditions are harsh and life-threatening."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Security personnel and police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Security personnel are known for their firm responses to what might be perceived as relatively minor issues. Avoid actions that might provoke them, such as taking photographs of them. If you’re stopped by the police, show respect and stay calm."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal among persons of at least 21 years old. However public attitudes are less tolerant than in the UK and showing affection in public may receive negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to collect, buy or export protected animals, plants or products made from them. This includes certain woods such as items made of rosewood. If you buy anything made of wild animal skin or shell, check with the vendor exactly what information you can give to customs if they ask for details."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stadiums and venues"]},{"k":"p","s":["Security and safety standards at stadiums and venues in Madagascar may be lower than in the UK. If you go to a large-scale event, make sure you know the location of fire exits and check exit routes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Madagascar, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You need to have both the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions vary greatly and are often poor. Many roads outside Antananarivo have steep gradients and sharp bends. Heavy freight trucks use the roads. Drive with extreme care as drivers often fail to signal and pull out sharply. Avoid driving at night as vehicles often have no lights and few roads are lit."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the rainy season, from December to April, many secondary roads are impassable except by 4-wheel-drive vehicles and bridges are often washed away."]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling in Madagascar be aware of the risks, including carjacking or robbery. If you are involved in, or see, an accident, you can call the police on 117. If you are driving and it is safe to do so, you can drive to the nearest town and report the incident to the police directly."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent road deaths involving multi-passenger taxi vans (‘taxi-brousses’ or ‘bush taxis’)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use pre-booked taxis or hotel transport. If you have concerns about the safety of a vehicle or the ability of a driver, ask for a different driver."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River and sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed criminals have boarded boats on the Tsiribihina River in western Madagascar and robbed the passengers. Seek alternative routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get local advice on ferries from Tamatave-Sonierana to Sainte Marie Island and the west coast (Toliara/Tuléar, Morondava, Mahajanga and Nosy Be). There have been accidents caused by overcrowding, poor maintenance, poor crew training and unexpected squalls. Check weather conditions locally before travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant risk of ",["piracy in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],". Pirates can attack up to 1,000 nautical miles from the Somali coast or more. If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The cyclone season in Madagascar normally runs from November to April. Coastal areas are particularly at risk. Storms can cut access to remote parts of the country and contaminate water supplies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Organization weather warnings for Madagascar","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/swi/index.html"],", Meteo Madagascar (French) or ",["Cyclone Océan Indien","https://www.cycloneoi.com/"]," (French, Malagasy)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["cyclone warnings","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Madagascar. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Central Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, over 30 people were killed when criminals (often referred to as ‘dahalo’) set fire to buildings in a village in Ankazobe District, north-west of Antananarivo. Armed forces are active in the area. Dahalo have not targeted tourists but you should seek local advice before travelling there."]},{"k":"h","s":["Northern Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use an official local guide if you’re visiting the Montagne des Français protected area. Take local advice if visiting beaches as there have been opportunistic attacks on tourists."]},{"k":"h","s":["Southern Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent incidents involving cattle rustlers (‘dahalo’) in southern Madagascar have resulted in fatalities. Tourists have not been targeted, but you should avoid staying in rural areas without security arrangements. Madagascar’s armed forces are active in southern Madagascar."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2021, a large-scale attack on 3 villages in Midongy District resulted in the deaths of 17 civilians and 2 military officers. Other attacks have taken place:"]},{"k":"li","s":["to the north of Fort Dauphin"]},{"k":"li","s":["around the township of Betroka"]},{"k":"li","s":["along the west coast between Belo sur Tsiribihina and Toliara (Tuléar)"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the Commune of Ilakakabe (near Isalo National Park)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in the southern triangle between Ihosy, Toliara (Tuléar) and Fort Dauphin remains tense, the risks are greater at night and the roads are in a poor condition. Use a recognised tour operator when travelling in this area. If you are travelling to Fort Dauphin, you should travel by air."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal gangs have attacked vehicles travelling in convoy on the RN7 (between Antananarivo and Toliara (Tuléar)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be vigilant when visiting night clubs in Toliara (Tuléar)."]},{"k":"p","s":["In July 2023, demonstrations in the Lanirano area to the east of Fort Dauphin turned violent with reports of gunfire and injury to civilians"]},{"k":"h","s":["Western Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of violent highway robberies, particularly at night, use a recognised tour operator when travelling in the region between Besalampy and Morombe, including the RN35 and RN1 (between Tsiroanomandidy and Maintirano). You should also maintain a high level of vigilance if you travel on the following roads: RN7, RN27, RN10 and RN34."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 117 from a mobile or 17 from a landline and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Madagascar","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/134/madagascar"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Madagascar","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/134/madagascar"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Madagascar. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tap water in Madagascar is unsafe. You should drink and use only boiled or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks. There are high levels of syphilis in Madagascar."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Madagascar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there are public and private hospitals in Antananarivo, they can only handle routine operations. For complex surgery, patients are flown to Mauritius, South Africa or Réunion. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Madagascar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/madagascar-doctors/list-of-medical-facilities-in-madagascar"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Madagascar"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ambulance or police emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 17"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mobile: 117"]},{"k":"p","s":["To contact the police station directly, call 19, or 119 from a mobile phone."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 18"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mobile: 118"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"h","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Madagascar"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Madagascar"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Madagascar"]," in Madagascar"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Madagascar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/madagascar-bereavement-information-pack/madagascar-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Madagascar","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/madagascar-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/madagascar/british-embassy-antananarivo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/madagascar/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":20356,"change":"New information on the presence of ‘Africa Corps’ in Madagascar (‘Safety and security’ page)."}};
